  "events": [],
  "notes": [
    "`time_stamp_ms` read in milliseconds, from its name and the ground station's clock: over the longest stretch of packets, 21.0 s of the ground station's clock, the board's advances 21.0 s read in milliseconds, 0.9992 for each second. The stamps in it keep within 2 s of one gap from the ground station's clock. The band is 0.8 to 1.25 over at least 20 s",
    "the board's clock runs in 2 stretches, each a steady gap from the ground station's clock, as after a restart of the board. Each is placed on the ground station's clock by its own median gap",
    "`Alt Info & Cfg.barometer_pressure` read in atmospheres, from its size and its step: its first value is 0.9707179665565491, a pad's pressure in atmospheres or bars if within 0.4935 to 1.1. A value counts as a whole number within its own rounding as sent. Of its 22 distinct non-zero values, 100.0% are a whole number of pascals divided by 101,325. Of the same values, 0.0% are a whole number of pascals divided by 100,000",
    "`Alt Info & Cfg.press_ref` read in atmospheres, from its size and the barometer's: its first value, 0.9707061648368835, is 0.001% from `barometer_pressure`'s in the same packet, 0.9707179665565491, read in atmospheres; atmospheres and bars are 1.3% apart",
    "`Position Data.fcb_altitude` read in meters, from the barometer and the coast: from `barometer_pressure`'s first value to its lowest, each within 0.5 s of a sample of the column, the standard atmosphere climbs 213.5 m. The column's climb over the same span is 213.5, 1.000 times that. Meters need within 25%. Over the coast, 6 samples across 5.0 s, the column's least-squares parabola slows it 9.81 m/s², 1.000 g read so. An upward coast slows at least 1 g. The band is a factor of 1.8 either way, where feet would read 3.28 times",
    "`Position Data.v_speed` read in meters per second, from the barometer and the coast: over the barometer's ascent, the standard atmosphere climbs 213.5 m. The ascent is the 7.0 s from where the barometer's pressure last began to fall to its lowest. The column integrates to 213.5, the speed taken as a straight line between samples up to 1.0 s apart. The climb is 1.000 times that. Meters per second need at least 10 m and within 25%. Over the coast, 8 samples across 7.0 s, the column's least-squares line slows it 9.84 m/s², 1.003 g read so. An upward coast slows at least 1 g. The band is a factor of 1.8 either way, where feet would read 3.28 times",
    "`Position Data.fcb_latitude` and `Position Data.fcb_longitude` kept as written, holding no fix: every position is (0, 0), the receiver's mark for none, or a gap",
    "`Groundstation Status.gs_lat` and `Groundstation Status.gs_lon` kept as written, holding no fix: every position is (0, 0), the receiver's mark for none, or a gap",
    "`Orientation.accel_x`, `Orientation.accel_y` and `Orientation.accel_z` kept as written, the pad's gravity and the barometer not both bearing meters per second squared out: the three axes' magnitude reads within 10% of 9.806 65 for 0.0 s of the file's time. It reads within 10% of 1 for 0.0 s. A board at rest or under a parachute reads 1 g. Meters per second squared need at least 1 s and twice the other's. The climb check can't be made: no launch: no sample reads 3 times the median of the 10 before it and the next two 2 times",
    "`Orientation.angle_vertical` kept as written, with no accelerometer read in m/s² to check it by: its values run from 0 to 0",
    "`Orientation.rot_vel_x`, `Orientation.rot_vel_y` and `Orientation.rot_vel_z` kept as written, with no accelerometer read in m/s²: their unit is checked against its gravity as the board turns",
    "`Position Data.temperature` kept as written, in degrees Celsius or Fahrenheit alike: its name states no unit, and nothing in the file tells the two apart; its values run from 19.5 to 19.5",
    "`Position Data.gps_alt` kept as written, with no check of its unit but the barometer's: a GPS altitude's rise against the barometer's tells meters from feet, but no second check independent of the barometer is in the file; its values run from 0 to 0",
    "`Position Data.fcb_battery_voltage` kept as written, in a unit nothing in the file checks: its name states no unit, and no check in the file reaches one; its values run from 7.599999904632568 to 7.599999904632568",
    "`Groundstation Status.gs_temp` kept as written, in degrees Celsius or Fahrenheit alike: its name states no unit, and nothing in the file tells the two apart; its values run from 27 to 27",
    "2 fields of the `Line Cutter Data` packets, such as `lc_state`, aren't ones this reader knows: their values are kept as written",
    "1 line is the ground station's own message, not a packet, \"Packet too short, 12 bytes\" on line 30: skipped",
    "the fields `callsign`, `lc_note`, `radio_name` hold text, not numbers: they are left out of the channels; `crc` decides which packets are read"
  ]
}
